course: dictionary
lesson: 2472
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. The word date is a good example. «The next crewed landing on the Moon is planned for the late 2020s, but dates for big space missions very often slip.» Here dates means planned times for things to happen, not fruit.
explain: Look at the words near date. In «Write the date at the top of your work», a date is the day, month and year. Ask: which meaning fits the clues around it? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases help you too. «Out of date» means old or no longer good to use, while «up to date» means new and current. A «use-by date» on food tells you when to stop eating it. Dates also show when things happened, in order on a timeline.
fact: A date is the day, month and year when something happens.
fact: A date is also a sweet brown fruit that grows on a palm tree.
fact: A date can be a plan to meet someone, often a romantic outing.
fact: To date something means to write the date on it, or to find out how old it is.
fact: Out of date means old or no longer good to use; up to date means new and current.
exercise: «Write the date at the top of your work.» What is a date here? | A type of palm tree | A plan to meet a friend | *The day, month and year | A sweet brown fruit
exercise: «Dates for big space missions very often slip.» What do dates mean in this sentence? | Sweet brown fruits | Names of the Moon | *Planned times when things will happen | Old, rotten food
exercise: What does «out of date» mean? | Written at the top of a page | *Old or no longer good to use | Brand new and shiny | Very hungry
test: «The use-by date is on the yogurt pot.» What does use-by date tell you? | The name of the shop | The price of the yogurt | The colour of the pot | *The last day it is safe to eat
test: Ella says, «I'll date the old photo to find its year.» What does date mean here? | Give a plan to meet someone | Hang it on a palm tree | Eat it like a sweet fruit | *Find out how old it is
exam: «Diwali falls on a different date each year.» Which meaning of date fits best? | A romantic outing | *The day when it happens | A sweet brown fruit | Out of date
